  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/freeze conditions tonight through Sunday \nnight.\n\nThe center of a large 1030 mb will settle just north of the Ohio \nRiver Valley by 12Z Sunday. As dry high pressure builds over the \nforecast area, the pressure gradient across SE GA/SC will decrease \ntonight. Winds could completely decouple across inland counties \ntonight, with light and variable winds across the coastal counties. \nShallow cumulus clouds across the region this afternoon should \ndissipate early this evening. REFS indicates that sky is expected to \nremain clear through late tonight, then thin high clouds sourced \nfrom the Southern Plains may reach SE GA around daybreak Sunday. \nGiven nearly optimal radiational cooling condition, the cooler \ntemperature guidance will be favored. Using a blend of cooler \nguidance, low temperatures are forecast to range from the upper 20s \ninland to mid 30s across the coastal counties away from the beaches. \nA Freeze Warning has been posted for inland SE GA/SC. A Frost \nAdvisory will be issued for coastal SC counties and the I-95 \ncorridor of SE GA. Hours of frost supporting temperatures should \nfavor widespread to areas of frost tonight.\n\nIf widespread freezing temperatures occur tonight into Sunday \nmorning, then this will end the local growing season and \nFrost/Freeze products will not be issued for Sunday night into \nMonday morning. However, if only some areas observe freezing \ntemperatures, then the growing season continues and we will likely \nneed Frost/Freeze products on Sunday night into Monday morning. \nRegardless of the outcome, overnight temperatures will be below \nnormal for this time of year.",
